6.5072\"","\"105.72566352\"","\"4.83420413723216707223934005914479978\"","\"20.3549534125257503706128106890510387\"","\"23.6403742009055844373637430823411035\"","\"6.58\"","true","\"146.96006352\"","\"14.4259525208104287733626511700958065\"","\"Zero; no distributions or dividend reinvestment modeled.\"","\"reported_FY26_equity\"","\"excluded_advance_tax_asset\"","\"excluded_prepaid_IPO_asset\"","\"excluded_DTA\"","\"debt_component_rounding_residual\"","\"modeled_opening_net_assets\"","\"identity\"","\".0592\"","\".0001\"","\"17.8382\"","\"18.2762 - .1961 - .1826 - .0592 - .0001 = 17.8382\"","\"Prepaid IPO cost is recovered once through the net cash fee bridge. Advance tax and DTA are not separately monetized. Modeled equity is a reduced operating balance, not a restatement of audited equity.\"","\"one_year_lagged_FY26_NOPAT_over_FY25_operating_IC\"","\"contemporaneous_FY26_ending_ROIC\"","\"commissioned_cohort_ROIC\"","\"0.248010733806001273130364159185196567\"","\"Lagged denominator mechanically excludes most FY26 property and stock investment and can overstate returns; it is not incremental or commissioned-cohort ROIC. Exact in-service dates, store-level NOPAT and productive inventory cohorts are unavailable, so a meaningful commissioned-capital return is ND.\"","\"source_priority\"","\"excluded\"","\"2026-10-20\"","\"id\"","\"title\"","\"url\"","\"locations\"","\"note\"","\"secondary\"","\"Riyaasat red herring prospectus,12 June2026\"","\"https://aibi.org.in/Current_DOC/26270048.pdf\"","\"6f256c0d6cc406e3775099284a529b5d0664ed7a4c3d5e4d030098ce2d733fd0\"","\"Printed24–37 risks;71auditor history;79–94capital;99–118objects;151–200business/history;229onwardrestatedstatements;annexures and notes read\"","\"Primary issuer prospectus hosted by investment-bank association. Printed pages generally PDFpage minus2.\"","\"DRHP25\"","\"Earlier draft prospectus, FY22 and initial history\"","\"https://www.sharekhan.com/MediaGalary/IPODocuments/PD0017F.pdf\"","\"de79b0de4b9fde990ed6b4cced58276677ad9bdaede845c1f846327ba557982f\"","\"Restated financial section and reconciliation notes\"","\"Primary issuer draft mirrored by broker; superseded by RHP for current terms.\"","\"AR2022\"","\"Original annual report FY2022\"","\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0780/2116/5367/files/Annual_Report_21-22.pdf?v=1746263749\"","\"53ab2a897b3c03ba4861717ccdb74c2b731c2f6bde8c5e688e1af2a27c491d5e\"","\"PDF14–18 audit;statements/notes thereafter\"","\"Original linked issuer annual-report page https://www.riyaasatlifestyle.in/pages/annual-report . FY22-24 original financial figures in thousands, FY25-26 lakh.\"","\"AR2023\"","\"Original annual report FY2023\"","\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0780/2116/5367/files/Annual_Report_22-23.pdf?v=1746263754\"","\"7dc289beb595d2266e2986c9900e61feb15cbcbeab9c8f42fb0c6ec68f4062a3\"","\"PDF16–27 audit,CARO,IFC;statements/notes thereafter\"","\"Original annual report FY2024\"","\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0780/2116/5367/files/Annual_Report_Riyaasat.pdf?v=1781874374\"","\"67d9bb914f52bb8ce27202c9460e07fb2f3b08d465be43a67c0c32aa1cc696ae\"","\"PDF14–25 audit,CARO,IFC;statements/notes thereafter\"","\"Original annual report FY2025\"","\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0780/2116/5367/files/Annual_Report_Riyaasat_2024-25.pdf?v=1781874269\"","\"e7322edb51441005197b33638abed6fb72f0aa2ca84273eda2d44737f8ce83eb\"","\"PDF14–24 audit,CARO,IFC,includingimage-onlyPDF16;statements/notes thereafter\"","\"AR2026\"","\"Original annual report FY2026\"","\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0780/2116/5367/files/Annual_report.pdf?v=1788778814\"","\"4308d815db1a0d57c61a55fd5def058d57841f084ee14f065bd1e92d85f06292\"","\"PDF54–68 audit/CARO/IFC;69–71statements;notes72–98\"","\"FY26 annual report as filed5September2026\"","\"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachHis/95e91031-ad8c-484b-824d-eb4463efff51.pdf\"","\"531b43ac0e05514485ab636791079c4e4f645c675a7b195b55dcd35faf5ee201\"","\"Full main audit/CARO/IFC PDF54–68, statements69–71,notes72–98\"","\"Primary BSE filing retrieved via BusinessStandard mirror https://bsmedia.business-standard.com/_media/bs/data/announcements/bse/05092026/95e91031-ad8c-484b-824d-eb4463efff51.pdf\"","\"1September2026 postal notice, changed IPO objects\"","\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0780/2116/5367/files/Postal_Ballot_Notice.pdf?v=1788248084\"","\"c0668ca7aa59480a98d999b21f915a9be8744c184d818a3e193140b407efec22\"","\"Explanatory statement, utilization and old/new project tables;fullnotice read\"","\"30September2026 property-acquisition disclosure\"","\"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachHis/eb3a0341-f571-481c-8e13-f60b4824c89a.pdf\"","\"5dd6ca94392908468ae0ab85e2aede93f12cfc70ddf40b91eb31d2353de703ff\"","\"Full two-page exchange disclosure\"","\"Mirror https://bsmedia.business-standard.com/_media/bs/data/announcements/bse/30092026/eb3a0341-f571-481c-8e13-f60b4824c89a.pdf\"","\"3October2026 voting/scrutinizer result\"","\"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachHis/5ad21c51-aa55-40a6-8664-c729f1b9beaa.pdf\"","\"f7f6e7ac775291cb8d93c9fb5c9005d19190c61018dc9a86a2d11729f29da728\"","\"Fullresult including shares and vote counts\"","\"Mirror https://bsmedia.business-standard.com/_media/bs/data/announcements/bse/03102026/5ad21c51-aa55-40a6-8664-c729f1b9beaa.pdf\"","\"VEDANT26\"","\"Vedant Fashions FY26 results presentation\"","\"https://vedantfashions.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Vedant-Fashion-Investor-presentation-_Q4-and-FY26.pdf\"","\"3c8ac9453efadd7b383ee1217514823cf59408dd257e5c41877facac9619ec1b\"","\"13–14operatingreach;19–21financials\"","\"Primarypeer,inINRmillion\"","\"GO26\"","\"Go Fashion FY26 annual report\"","\"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachHis/db7dd743-8b50-4a62-af3b-8d160e2018a7.pdf\"","\"0eb57dfffe84a052903b926f83e3b9945e76d3b264197b75d210c474d36e449c\"","\"FY26financialstatements,cashflow,equitybuyback,noteinventory\"","\"Mirror https://bsmedia.business-standard.com/_media/bs/data/announcements/bse/17082026/db7dd743-8b50-4a62-af3b-8d160e2018a7.pdf\"","\"SAI26\"","\"Sai Silks Kalamandir FY26 annual report\"","\"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachHis/2c603061-cb88-4f0f-87a4-0e9ba5ccbf78.pdf\"","\"476470608017a6c5ef02ac6d9dc7a7e63230a5e9f83fe7290f3b30f3e2d87749\"","\"Auditedfinancials,cashflow,MD&A\"","\"Mirror https://bsmedia.business-standard.com/_media/bs/data/announcements/bse/17072026/2c603061-cb88-4f0f-87a4-0e9ba5ccbf78.pdf\"","\"Secondary reference price\"","\"₹98.4,19Octclose\"","\"Not executable quote, rounded\"","\"security_extract.json\"","\"The two matching issuer records in the 19 October 2026 NSE interoperability master. This is metadata, not a BSE trading-history extract.\"","\"peer_market_extract.json\"","\"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/content/cm/BhavCopy_NSE_CM_0_0_0_20261019_F_0000.csv.zip\"","\"f0a2e9bf7cb185bb112704355772d2954d662abee3d7295414aabc26d6ecfbde\"","\"Exact selected records retained in authored extract\"","\"Original exchange/issuer disclosures first; opinion and management claims separated; market secondary reference explicitly downgraded. No post-cutoff operating result imported.\"","\"RawPDFs,OCR,HTML,screenshots,private transfer data and helpers excluded from deliverables.\"","\"scope\"","\"issues\"","\"not_established\"","\"positive_controls\"","\"gate_conclusion\"","\"Standalone Indian Accounting Standards (AS), not IndAS; no subsidiary/JV/associate company per FY26 directors report. The full original FY22-FY26 main audit, available CARO and IFC reports were read, not just the unmodified-opinion headline.\"","\"year\"","\"auditor\"","\"main\"","\"CARO\"","\"IFC\"","\"emphasis\"","\"FY22\"","\"Arpan Chudgar & Associates\"","\"2022-09-05\"","\"AR2022 PDF14–18\"","\"Unmodified\"","\"Stated not applicable\"","\"Exempt per report\"","\"Going-concern paragraph says management identifying plans to improve but explicitly no uncertainty. Do not describe this as a material-uncertainty conclusion.\"","\"23 October 2021 to 31 March 2022 incorporation stub; original report has no cash-flow statement.\"","\"financial_quality\"","\"2023-08-29\"","\"AR2023 PDF16–27\"","\"Same unusual no-uncertainty going-concern emphasis.\"","\"Inventory verification positive. Dhagaa loan, all directors partners, without stipulated repayment/interest schedule. No fraud/default/resignation reported for financial year. CARO no lender borrowing conflicts with original note5 promoter-relative borrowing101.7809lakh.\"","\"Original Dhagaa advance was ₹174 lakh, about 79% of original equity of ₹221.5298 lakh. Receivable, payable and cash-flow comparative vintages differ materially and are retained.\"","\"other_matter\"","\"Abhishek Kumar & Associates\"","\"2024-08-28\"","\"AR2024 PDF14–25\"","\"Going-concern emphasis explicitly says no uncertainty.\"","\"No accounting software audit-trail feature, while opinion remains unmodified.\"","\"Inventory verification positive. No unsecured loans assertion followed by on-demand loan assertions, unresolved boilerplate inconsistency. No fraud/default/resignation reported.\"","\"Original CFO of −₹346.3378 lakh differs from the FY25 comparative of −₹242.15 lakh and RHP restated −₹272.76 lakh. The original investing subtotal erroneously includes CFO; the cash roll reconciles using actual PPE outflow of ₹32.8577 lakh.\"","\"2025-09-04\"","\"AR2025 PDF14–24 including image-onlyPDF16 and visualaudit-trailPDF18\"","\"Audit-trail paragraph says has not used suitable software, then says same operated throughout year, internally contradictory.\"","\"Bank quarterly statements disagree with books; inventory verification positive; no fraud/default/resignation reported; no one-year inability-to-meet-liabilities uncertainty identified, not assurance of viability.\"","\"audit_trail\"","\"2026-07-21\"","\"AR26_BSE PDF54–68; notes96–98\"","\"Positive audit-trail reporting in main report; does not erase prior negatives or inventory maintained outside Tally Prime.\"","\"Physical inventory verification impracticable; auditor unable to comment on coverage/procedure/discrepancies. Bank quarterly statements still disagree with books due to unreconciled/classification balances. Disputed income tax118.12lakh. No fraud/default/wilful-default or current-year auditor resignation reported; no one-year material uncertainty indicated.\"","\"finding\"","\"evidence\"","\"materiality\"","\"contrary\"","\"consequence\"","\"A1\"","\"Inventory verification and system coverage\"","\"FY26 inventory of ₹41.0462cr exceeds revenue of ₹33.3746cr. CARO limits physical verification; note33 says inventory is outside Tally Prime.\"","\"A 10% inventory haircut is ₹4.10462cr, about22.46% of reported equity; a20% haircut is ₹8.20924cr, about44.92%, before tax.\"","\"Main/IFC opinions unmodified; earlier inventory physical-verification clauses positive.\"","\"G2 remains Hold and CAP/EARN NS. Obtain SKU age, movement, cost/NRV, physical counts and an independent reconciliation.\"","\"A2\"","\"Recurring bank-versus-books reconciliation gaps\"","\"FY25 and FY26 CARO report bank-to-book mismatches. FY26 note32 says drawing power is based on receivables/payables, not inventory.\"","\"Not cured by assuming inventory alone determines drawing power. Could affect facility headroom/covenants, but no actual default disclosed.\"","\"G2 and G3 Hold; require signed monthly reconciliations and sanctioned/used/undrawn limits.\"","\"A3\"","\"Audit-trail and document consistency\"","\"FY24 has a negative audit-trail Other Matter; FY25 wording is contradictory; FY26 main reporting is positive.\"","\"Evidence of historical control weakness, not proof that all entries are false. Verify remediation and separate inventory system integration.\"","\"A4\"","\"Related-party balances and old funding\"","\"Original FY23 Dhagaa advance ₹174 lakh versus equity ₹221.5298 lakh lacked a repayment/interest schedule. RHP January2026 RPT receivables total ₹378.47 lakh does not sum the listed ₹31.67 + ₹9.21 + ₹2.09 = ₹42.97 lakh. FY25 RPT receivables ₹182.28 lakh exceed total trade AR ₹68.05 lakh, suggesting advance/classification overlap.\"","\"Do not add these summaries again to balance-sheet assets. Seek counterparty terms, settlement and classification schedules. No automatic diversion allegation.\"","\"A5\"","\"Auditor succession chronology\"","\"RHP printed71 records a6 June2023 resignation for preoccupation and a3 July appointment effective1 July, while the predecessor signed the original FY23 opinion on29 August2023.\"","\"Retain exact dates; no current-year resignation is not no historical resignation. Appointment/resignation filings and signing chronology unresolved.\"","\"A6\"","\"Intermediary representation malformed\"","\"FY26 note39 has malformed affirmative fund-routing wording, while the main auditor’s management representation is negative. An IPO table interrupts the text.\"","\"Unresolved wording/document inconsistency, not established fund diversion. Seek corrected note and signed confirmation.\"","\"A7\"","\"IPO shares and cash reconciliation\"","\"The CARO table combines net-offer count2,702,400 at₹106 with gross proceeds. Full fresh shares2,848,800 include146,400 market-maker shares, producing ₹30.19728cr.\"","\"Use10,744,478 current shares. Include IPO cash once, after fees and with restricted-use pools.\"","\"A8\"","\"Cash-flow and vintage controls\"","\"FY26 cash-generated line−₹1,258.03 lakh is the working-capital subtotal. Operating profit₹1,049.43 lakh less tax₹110.73 lakh reconciles reported CFO−₹319.32 lakh within rounding. Net investing−₹2,650.72 lakh includes other noncurrent release₹623.36 lakh.\"","\"This is a label error, not a failed final-CFO arithmetic identity. FY25 capital advance₹480 lakh in other current liabilities becomeszero; retain the cash effect without adding it again to capex.\"","\"A9\"","\"Governance presentation and remuneration\"","\"Corporate information mislabels Sobhanaben as independent; relationship disclosures identify her as the MD’s mother and WTD’s spouse. Director remuneration₹46 lakh and rent/commission₹66.40 lakh are disclosed. KMP table totals and CSR note₹15 lakh versus P&L₹12.90 lakh require reconciliation.\"","\"Use substantive relationships, not template labels, in assessing independence. Routine RPTs are not automatically abusive.\"","\"A10\"","\"Post-IPO project commitment escalation\"","\"Original four-store fitout/deposits₹13.5503cr versus revised comparable₹19.2395cr and a separate₹15.5cr owned property. The revised headline₹20.8127cr includes₹1.5732cr annual rent, unlike the original budget.\"","\"Cash commitments exceed the unchanged IPO store allocation. Do not double count rent. Current funding remains unverified.\"","\"A11\"","\"Tax and other senior claims\"","\"Opening current-tax provision₹2.1289cr, excluded advance-tax asset₹0.1961cr and disputed claim₹1.1812cr are separate balances.\"","\"The model settles the opening claim gross, does not invent an offset and separately stresses the dispute. Audit liquidity wording is not a project-funding guarantee.\"","\"Fraud or siphoning\"","\"Actual bank default\"","\"Current-year statutory auditor resignation\"","\"Actual cash shortfall as at19 October2026\"","\"Recoverable inventory liquidation value\"","\"Current promoter encumbrances or a comprehensive post-listing dilutive-instrument registry\"","\"Original annual audits are available from incorporation through FY26.\"","\"Main and available IFC opinions are unmodified.\"","\"FY26 main audit-trail reporting is positive.\"","\"No fraud, default or wilful default is reported.\"","\"The IPO object variation was approved through a postal ballot.\"","\"The issuer disclosed the property acquisition as non-related-party.\"","\"Hold—unresolved, not Avoid—fraud. Accounting and funding uncertainties block scoreable IAS and investable ranking until reconciled.\"","\"name\"","\"prior_revenue\"","\"lease_cash\"","\"shares_basis\"","\"close\"","\"same_store_gro